  "behavior_evidence": [
    "Twenty native rows cover all four overloads, head/middle/tail insertion, growth/no-growth, empty, invalid before/after indices, each backward-shift failure phase, donor copy/move failure and growth followed by insertion failure.",
    "Growing first copies all old values because the native move constructor can throw, destroys old values in order, then shifts through move-construction and immediate source destruction backwards. Rust takes separate relocation/shift/value callbacks without Clone/Default bounds.",
    "Callbacks mutate move sources before throwing. Rows preserve original Size, exact live/dead slot bitmap, values/resources, unpublished live tail, donor state, buffer identity and moved payload identity. Rust source destruction also checks actual slot addresses.",
    "Native and Rust fixtures repair only dead prefix slots and destroy an unregistered live tail before ordinary cleanup. Strict Miri has no leaks or provenance failures; ordinary safe insertion remains unchanged.",
    "Raw placement construction and destruction are shared with DynamicArray through one private helper; three existing DynamicArray raw-lifetime/replacement/retained-parameter regression suites pass under Rust and strict Miri.",
    "Original NonTrivialType insertion now invokes the explicit callback adapter with nonpanicking String moves; its original values/assertions are preserved.",
    "Previous Erase library rejects missing APIs while candidate runs them. Covariance and Send/Sync/Unpin/unwind traits stay unchanged. Separate tests cover borrowed elements and safe invalid insertion ownership."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These adapters are unsafe: native shift/value constructor exceptions can leave registered dead slots and a live unpublished tail. Caller must suppress automatic Drop, track progress, repair every dead prefix slot and destroy a live extra tail before any safe element access or normal Drop. This is not safe exception parity.",
    "Destructors must not unwind; constructors must leave valid source objects even on unwind. No address-dependent in-place construction is promised by a callback returning T.",
    "Failed growth retains existing reserve_with_relocation cleanup policy; native growth exception leaks/partial state are not claimed.",
    "Protected shiftRight arbitrary counts/subranges and trivial memmove policy are not included; existing safe convenience Insert methods retain Rust ownership semantics.",
    "Allocator hooks, ABI layout, zero-size native equivalence, writable aliases and metadata observation through aliases remain outside this receipt.",
    "No global API/test ledger changed; class/kernel full parity is not established."
  ],
  "remaining_callable_work": [
    "Audit LinearVector remaining constructors, Assign/Resize/Append/Emplace native element operations and protected storage helpers against precise compiler declarations."
  ],
